         recommended test: For every plausible defect the review enumerates, the run includes a corresponding injected edit.
           inputs:  A review/pipeline run with at least one plausible defect that is enumerated in the review state but does not appear in any killed mutation attempt, alongside another defect that does appear in a killed attempt. Use routing enabled so `pairs_not_worth_asking(...)` is consulted, and ensure the enumerated-but-never-killed defect has at least one candidate test that would be skipped if the map were built from plausible defects rather than attempts.
           detects: The skipped-pair map is derived only from killed mutation attempts, so any plausible defect that is enumerated but never appears in a killed attempt contributes no injected edit at all.
